  "title": "Zdravlje",
  "titleEn": "Health",
  "grammarTip": "Trebati, morati, and moći are the three core modal verbs. Morati expresses strict obligation ('moram uzeti lijek' — I must take medicine); moći expresses ability or permission ('mogu li zakazati termin?' — can I book an appointment?); trebati expresses need and can be personal ('trebam ići kod ljekara' — I need to go to the doctor) or impersonal with the dative ('treba mi lijek' — I need medicine, literally 'medicine is needed to me').",
